      "content": "it's just so exhausting. sitting in the emptiness is even harder than trying to fix things, because you realize there's nowhere to go. if the game is rigged and everything is just a distraction, then what is the actual \"honest\" end point? like, if everything is hollow, does it even make sense to keep trying to exist in this emptiness? it feels like i'm just waiting for a crash that's already happened.",
